<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TURKU, Finland 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the ice hockey</p>
<p>world championships on Friday:</p>
<p>Pool B (in Turku)</p>
<p>Italy 2 Norway 2 (2-0 0-0 0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Italy - Bruno Zarrillo (9:00), Bob Nardella (12:47)</p>
<p>Norway - Ole Elkild Dahlstrom (57:58), Atle Alexander Olsen (</p>
<p>58:47)</p>
<p>Penalties: Italy 20 minutes, Norway 20</p>
<p>Attendance: 3,657</p>
<p>Pool A (in Helsinki)</p>
<p>France 2 Germany 1 (1-0 1-0 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>France - Roger Dube (03:22, 35:15).</p>
<p>Germany - Marco Sturm (42:15).</p>
<p>Penalties: France 12 minutes, Germany 14 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,205.</p>
<p>Pool B (in Turku) Sweden 1 Latvia 1 (0-0 0-0 1-1) Scorers: Sweden - Jorgen Jonsson (57:39) Latvia - Igors Pavlovs (41:27) Penalties: Sweden 10 minutes, Latvia 10 Attendance: 4,470  </p>
<p>Pool A</p>
<p>Finland 5 Slovakia 2 (1-0 1-1 3-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Finland - Juha Lind (14:55), Mika Nieminen (27:28, 49:43),</p>
<p>Kai Nurminen (44:17), Teppo Numminen (54:19).</p>
<p>Slovakia - Lubomir Kolnik (37:31), Jiri Bicek (47:26).</p>
<p>Penalties: Finland 6 minutes, Slovakia 10 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,367.</p>
